`plone-client login NAME --browser` prints the URL of the site's login page, to open in the browser you log in with (or opens it with `--open`), and waits on `127.0.0.1` for the token, which the site's frontend hands over once the user allows it, for sites whose people log in through another provider. The MCP server offers the same login as a `login` tool, so an assistant can renew an expired login: it gives the URL to open, then stores the token. It needs a frontend that supports a loopback `return_url`, such as volto-authomatic once collective/volto-authomatic#50 is released. @ericof
